infographic list-column-simple-vertical-arrow
data
  title Validation timing: what each policy punishes
  desc Validation can run continuously — the policy only decides when the verdict is shown, and each pure choice injures someone
  lists
    - label onChange from the first keystroke
      desc Yells while the user is mid-thought: every field reads invalid until it is finished, and premature red lands as rejection — the session-replay cause of form abandonment.
    - label onSubmit only
      desc Punishes trust: ten fields of effort, then a wall of errors at once, often with the first broken field scrolled off-screen above the fold.
    - label onBlur
      desc The fair verdict — leaving a field signals the user is done with it, so judging then is fair. The compromise field UX research keeps landing on.
    - label Hybrid: reward early, punish late
      desc Validate at first blur; once a field is touched and in error, re-check on change so fixes clear instantly; re-run the full schema on submit and move focus to the first failure.
theme
  palette #f43f5e #f59e0b #6366f1 #14b8a6
